# qa-review — the reviewer gate on every PR that touches the QA suite.
#
# OPTIONAL. The everyday gate is local: /qa-warden:review writes a hash-pinned .reviewed marker and
# /qa-warden:doctor Check 15 flags any test reviewed before its last change. Use this workflow only
# when you need a gate nobody can skip. Rename to qa-review.yml to enable.
#
# This is the companion to qa-nightly.yml.example:
# the nightly REPLAYS the suite ($0 LLM); this one REVIEWS new/changed tests (one LLM call
# per PR). The reviewer is the gate that blocks green-but-wrong tests, and its competence is
# not the gap — its TRIGGERING is. A gate nobody runs blocks nothing.
#
# After enabling, mark the `qa-review` job a REQUIRED STATUS CHECK in branch protection.
# That is the only attestation an agent cannot forge: a PR touching tests/ or specs/ then
# cannot merge without the reviewer having run. (skills/review/SKILL.md §"CI wiring".)
#
# ── PREREQUISITE: the runner must be able to INSTALL the QA Warden plugin ──────────────────
# The `reviewer` subagent ships INSIDE the plugin. A bare runner has no plugin, so without
# the two inputs below the prompt asks for a subagent that does not exist and the review is
# done by an un-instructed model — which reads like a review and gates nothing.
# `plugin_marketplaces` takes a GIT URL, so the marketplace (the repo holding
# .claude-plugin/marketplace.json) must be pushed somewhere the runner can clone.
# A marketplace that exists only as a local directory CANNOT be used from CI.
name: qa-review
on:
  pull_request:
    paths: ['tests/**', 'specs/**', 'page-objects/**', 'fixtures/**']
jobs:
  qa-review:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    timeout-minutes: 30
    permissions:
      contents: read
      pull-requests: read
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
        with: { fetch-depth: 0 }        # full history so origin/<base>...HEAD resolves
      - uses: anthropics/claude-code-action@v1
        with:
          anthropic_api_key: ${{ secrets.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY }}
          # REPLACE with the Git URL of YOUR copy of the marketplace repo (see PREREQUISITE).
          plugin_marketplaces: |
            https://github.com/<your-org>/<qa-toolkit-marketplace-repo>.git
          plugins: |
            qa-warden@qa-toolkit
          prompt: >-
            Use the reviewer subagent to review the PR diff and its imported page objects.
            If no subagent named reviewer is available, fail the job and say the QA Warden plugin
            did not load — do NOT review the diff yourself.
            Fail the job on any reviewer FAIL, and also fail the job if the reviewer's report
            contains no explicit verdict line (a report cut off before a verdict is written
            is not a PASS).
